164
00:14:39,970 --> 00:14:41,150
How did we...

165
00:14:43,050 --> 00:14:44,980
I could do it then.

166
00:14:47,050 --> 00:14:50,610
So I should be able to do it now.

167
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,190
What do I do? I have to...

168
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,920
You really want to go to that place.

169
00:14:58,450 --> 00:15:00,690
You really want to meet that person.

170
00:15:01,350 --> 00:15:03,330
You must meet him wherever he is.

171
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:05,710
The feeling of wanting to go there

172
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:07,690
and the feeling of wanting
to see that person,

173
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:10,540
enlarge it and expand it.

174
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,300
Believe in it.

175
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:15,030
Believe that when you open your eyes,

176
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:17,100
you'll be there.

177
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:19,520
You'll meet the person you want to see.

178
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:27,440
Whatever.

179
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,460
Let's just try it.

180
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:34,920
Let's go.

181
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:46,400
Let me see Pu.

182
00:15:48,430 --> 00:15:52,390
Let me see Pu.

183
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,190
Let me see Pu.

184
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:18,570
I did it.

185
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,550
I actually did it.

186
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:26,090
Pu.

187
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:29,040
Hold on.

188
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:31,680
I'll bring you back soon.

189
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:27,730
Prepare a CT scan
for patient 702 right away.

190
00:17:27,859 --> 00:17:29,450
Okay, I'll get right on it.

191
00:17:31,210 --> 00:17:32,620
Senior.

192
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:33,940
Madam, why are you here?

193
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,120
I thought you went home.

194
00:17:35,210 --> 00:17:36,270
I overheard

195
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,980
that you're preparing a CT scan for 702.

196
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:39,080
Did something happen?

197
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:40,980
He's one of the first ones
infected at Minshin Road.

198
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:42,160
He's awake now.

199
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:44,230
He's awake? Really?

200
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:45,110
It's true.

201
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,050
I have to go. Let's talk later.

202
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:05,790
You mean the girl not only saw Kakarayan,

203
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,460
but she saw Toem too?

204
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:09,050
And Toem stabbed Kakarayan with a knife?

205
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,740
What on earth is going on?

206
00:18:14,150 --> 00:18:15,510
Tien-ti also told me

207
00:18:16,530 --> 00:18:18,590
that Toem wanted her
to tell me she's sorry.

208
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:21,060
"Sorry"?

209
00:18:22,690 --> 00:18:23,700
Why?

210
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:25,330
I mean we, the Kawas,

211
00:18:25,410 --> 00:18:27,130
do not feel regret.

212
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,550
Or is it because she's not a Kawas?

213
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:31,000
No way. That crazy woman

214
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:33,420
couldn't have said she's sorry.

215
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,950
This wasn't the first time
she has apologized to me.

216
00:18:40,110 --> 00:18:41,120
I remember last time

217
00:18:41,210 --> 00:18:43,230
before I returned to being the messenger,

218
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:45,390
I was lying on the floor.

219
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,810
She was holding the Comb of Memories

220
00:18:48,030 --> 00:18:49,830
and was about to alter my memories.

221
00:18:50,410 --> 00:18:51,680
She whispered in my ear.

222
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:53,400
She said,

223
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:54,850
"I'm sorry.

224
00:18:55,860 --> 00:18:58,550
This is the last time I'm lying to you."

225
00:19:01,670 --> 00:19:02,810
I don't know why.

226
00:19:03,650 --> 00:19:04,570
Those words

227
00:19:05,810 --> 00:19:07,040
and that scene

228
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:08,890
didn't seem...

229
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:11,790
It didn't seem like
it was the first time it had happened.

230
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:16,580
What do you mean?

231
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,820
People whose memories
have been altered by me

232
00:19:22,480 --> 00:19:24,420
would experience this sometimes.

233
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:26,660
It's like they experienced it,

234
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:29,830
but they're unsure if it really happened.

235
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,410
So I was thinking

236
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,350
if my memory

237
00:19:34,490 --> 00:19:37,090
had also been altered before.

238
00:19:40,610 --> 00:19:43,730
I suspect that you might not be
the only Kawas

239
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:45,670
whose memories had been altered.

240
00:19:48,530 --> 00:19:49,360
I think

241
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,430
the entire Cause and Effect
Correction Bureau,

242
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:53,980
you, my wife,

243
00:19:54,070 --> 00:19:55,170
and even me,

244
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:58,250
everything we believed to be true

245
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:01,730
might just be a lie someone made up.

246
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,260
[Rabies]

247
00:20:18,270 --> 00:20:18,890
Hello?

248
00:20:19,370 --> 00:20:21,000
[Hsieh Tien-ti, where are you?]

249
00:20:22,050 --> 00:20:23,510
I had something to take care of.
What's the matter?

250
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:24,740
[Listen.]

251
00:20:24,830 --> 00:20:26,850
[Pu's mom just called me.]

252
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:27,910
[She said]

253
00:20:28,210 --> 00:20:29,450
[Pu is awake.]

254
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:33,490
[Hsieh Tien-ti, what's the matter?]

255
00:20:33,850 --> 00:20:35,560
[Why does it seem like]

256
00:20:35,650 --> 00:20:37,320
[you're not very happy that Pu woke up?]

257
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:38,640
That's not true.

258
00:20:38,730 --> 00:20:40,580
I'm very happy, okay?

259
00:20:40,670 --> 00:20:42,820
[Okay, I'll talk to you later.]

260
00:20:42,910 --> 00:20:44,670
[I need to tell my mom the good news.]

261
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,550
[Bye.]

262
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:59,190
I really cured Pu.

263
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,270
Ai-ting.

264
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:20,530
Is it my turn?

265
00:21:24,530 --> 00:21:25,500
You can just tell me.

266
00:21:25,590 --> 00:21:27,700
Will I have my eyesight back?

267
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:31,620
I've done so many tests in the past weeks.

268
00:21:31,750 --> 00:21:33,510
They didn't help in any way.

269
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:35,840
My eyes won't heal, right?

270
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:39,320
It's not that. I'm here

271
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,000
